      "message": "There\u0027s a nightly feature called `never` (https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/primitive.never.html#infinite-loops), for which this could be written to return `Result\u003c!, Error\u003e`, but that\u0027s not available officially yet (and we don\u0027t allow nightly features in Android). Instead, I think the current best practice is to return `Option\u003cError\u003e` instead. @mmaurer@google.com - can you think of any better way of handling this case?",
